      "role": "user",
      "content": "Product of Array Except Self\n\nGiven an integer array nums, return an array answer such that answer[i] equals the product of all elements of nums except nums[i]. You must write an O(n) algorithm without using division.\n\nExample: nums = [1,2,3,4] -> [24,12,8,6].\nConstraints: 2 <= len(nums) <= 10^5.",
      "id": "m-0",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-13T12:17:43.630Z",
      "durationMs": 0
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "channel": "analysis",
      "content": "Complexity check: one pass, O(n) time, O(n) auxiliary space for the map. That meets the constraint.\n\nKey invariant: the data structure state after processing prefix i fully determines the answer for i+1.",
      "id": "m-1",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-13T12:17:43.872Z",
      "durationMs": 7869,
      "stepIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "channel": "commentary",
      "content": "",
      "toolCalls": [
        {
          "id": "call-1",
          "name": "run_tests",
          "arguments": "{\"language\":\"python3\",\"code\":\"class Solution:\\n    def productExceptSelf(self, nums: list[int]) -> list[int]:\\n        n = len(nums)\\n        out = [1] * n\\n        left = 1\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            left *= nums[i]\\n            out[i] = left\\n        right = 1\\n        for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\\n            out[i] *= right\\n            right *= nums[i]\\n        return out\"}",
          "parsedArguments": {
            "language": "python3",
            "code": "class Solution:\n    def productExceptSelf(self, nums: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n        n = len(nums)\n        out = [1] * n\n        left = 1\n        for i in range(n):\n            left *= nums[i]\n            out[i] = left\n        right = 1\n        for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n            out[i] *= right\n            right *= nums[i]\n        return out"
          }
        }
      ],
